  "facts": [
    "The Ship Canal Bridge, completed in 1961 and opened December 18, 1962, spans 4,429 feet across Portage Bay, making it the largest double‑deck steel truss bridge in the Northwest at its debut.",
    "Standing 182 feet above the canal, the bridge’s upper deck carries bidirectional traffic while the lower deck switches directions—southbound mornings, northbound afternoons—an early example of reversible express lanes.",
    "At 119 feet wide, the upper deck of the Ship Canal Bridge was engineered to accommodate Interstate 5’s growing traffic demands, a design that still supports the corridor’s critical north‑south flow."
